<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Persian War (1804–1813)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1813</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Persian War of 1804–1813 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> annexed eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Despite the efforts of Crown Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-mirza">Abbas Mirza</a> to build a modern army, Iran was defeated, notably at Aslanduz in 1812, and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-gulistan">Treaty of Gulistan</a> of 1813 it gave up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, Georgia and most of the khanates of the eastern Caucasus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1804-1813.jpg" alt="Russo-Persian War (1804–1813)" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Roubaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Livebridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
